From: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sound/soc/rockchip: add rv1106 i2s-tdm compatible

The rv1106/rv1103 SoC uses the same i2s-tdm controller as rv1126 but
doesn't require the rv1126 soc_data (softrst/grf config). Without a match
table entry the i2s driver never binds to ffae0000.i2s, which causes
asoc-simple-card to loop forever on -EPROBE_DEFER waiting for the DAI
component to appear.

Match with NULL .data, consistent with rk3588 and the vendor 5.10 kernel
which also has no soc_data for rv1106.

---
 sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s_tdm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s_tdm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s_tdm.c
@@ -1057,6 +1057,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id rockchip_i2s_tdm_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "rockchip,rk3568-i2s-tdm", .data = &rk3568_i2s_soc_data },
 	{ .compatible = "rockchip,rk3588-i2s-tdm" },
 	{ .compatible = "rockchip,rv1126-i2s-tdm", .data = &rv1126_i2s_soc_data },
+	{ .compatible = "rockchip,rv1106-i2s-tdm" },
 	{},
 };
